   "evidence": "Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/LogDeriv.lean:149 has only `logDeriv_comp_neg`; no `logDeriv_comp_const_sub` exists in Mathlib. The chain appears at Data/LogDeriv.lean:40, Data/LogDeriv.lean:51 and RiemannZeta/FunctionalEquation.lean:42, and before this PR at Zeros/Completion/Dirichlet/LogDeriv.lean:96.",
   "file": "TauCeti/NumberTheory/LFunctions/Data/LogDeriv.lean",
   "fix": "Add `logDeriv_comp_const_sub (f : \ud835\udd5c \u2192 \ud835\udd5c') (a x : \ud835\udd5c) : logDeriv (fun z \u21a6 f (a - z)) x = -logDeriv f (a - x)`, a companion to Mathlib's `logDeriv_comp_neg`. Use it in `HasFunctionalEquation.logDeriv_eventuallyEq`, `HasFunctionalEquation.logDeriv_eq` and `logDeriv_completedRiemannZeta_one_sub`. Optionally also use it in the existing Dirichlet proof.",
   "issue": "The rewrite chain `logDeriv_apply, logDeriv_apply, deriv_comp_const_sub, neg_div` recomputes `logDeriv (fun z \u21a6 f (1 - z)) z = -logDeriv f (1 - z)` inline. The same chain appears again at line 50 of this file and at `TauCeti/NumberTheory/LSeries/RiemannZeta/FunctionalEquation.lean:41-42`. That is three copies of one reusable fact, written as a brittle chain of named rewrites.",
   "line": 39
  }
